<a id="Using_an_Inline_Checkstyle_Checker_Configuration"></a>

# Inline Checkstyle Checker Configuration

You can define a [Checker configuration](https://checkstyle.org/config.html#Checker) directly in the `<configuration>` section of the plugin in your `pom.xml`.
You then need no separate ruleset file, no separate project for your Checkstyle rules, and no parent POM structure.

Use the `checkstyleRules` parameter to define the checker configuration inside your `pom.xml`:

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-checkstyle-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <executions>
          <execution>
            <id>verify-style</id>
            <phase>process-classes</phase>
            <goals>
              <goal>check</goal>
            </goals>
          </execution>
        </executions>
        <configuration>
          <logViolationsToConsole>true</logViolationsToConsole>
          <checkstyleRules>
            <module name="Checker">

              <!-- Checks for size violations.                    -->
              <!-- See https://checkstyle.org/checks/sizes/       -->
              <module name="FileLength">
                <property name="max" value="3500" />
                <property name="fileExtensions" value="java"/>
              </module>

              <!-- Checks for whitespace.                         -->
              <!-- See https://checkstyle.org/checks/whitespace/  -->
              <module name="FileTabCharacter"/>

              <module name="TreeWalker">
                <module name="StaticVariableName"/>
                <module name="TypeName">
                  <property name="format" value="^_?[A-Z][a-zA-Z0-9]*$"/>
                </module>
              </module>
            </module>
          </checkstyleRules>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
  ...
</project>
```

<a id="Using_a_different_header"></a>

${esc.h}${esc.h} Different Header

The plugin writes the inline configuration to `target/checkstyle-checker.xml` and passes that file to Checkstyle.
The file starts with a [document type declaration](https://checkstyle.org/config.html#Configuration_XML_Structure), which the plugin adds for you.
The default declaration references the Checkstyle configuration DTD 1.3:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE module PUBLIC "-//Checkstyle//DTD Checkstyle Configuration 1.3//EN"
        "https://checkstyle.org/dtds/configuration_1_3.dtd">
```

DTD 1.3 is the current version, and the default works when you [upgrade Checkstyle at runtime](./upgrading-checkstyle.html).
Set the `checkstyleRulesHeader` parameter only if you need a different declaration:

```xml
<configuration>
  <checkstyleRules>
    ...
  </checkstyleRules>
  <checkstyleRulesHeader>
<![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE module PUBLIC "-//Checkstyle//DTD Checkstyle Configuration 1.3//EN"
        "https://checkstyle.org/dtds/configuration_1_3.dtd">
]]>
  </checkstyleRulesHeader>
</configuration>
```
